-- title:
--   Adelic Riemann–Roch from existence of the Stichtenoth genus
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ and $F$ be fields with $F$ a $K$-algebra satisfying `IsCurveOver K F`, that is: every nonzero $f \in F$ has a divisor whose coefficient at each place $v$ is $v.\mathrm{ord}\, f$ and whose degree is $0$; each place has residue field finite over $K$; and $\Omega_{F/K}$ is free of rank one over $F$. Assume `StichtenothGenusExists K F`: there is at least one place of $F/K$, the Riemann–Roch space $L(0)$ is finite-dimensional over $K$, and there are $\gamma_0 \in \mathbb{Z}$ and a divisor $D_0$ with $L(D_0)$ finite-dimensional, $\deg D_0 - \ell(D_0) = \gamma_0 - 1$, and $\deg D - \ell(D) \le \gamma_0 - 1$ for every divisor $D$. Here divisors are finitely supported $\mathbb{Z}$-valued functions on places, $\deg$ is the sum of coefficients weighted by the residue degrees, and $\ell(D) = \dim_K L(D)$. The conclusion asserts the existence of an integer $\gamma$ such that for every divisor $D$: first, the quotient of the adele space $\mathbb{A} = \sup_E \{\alpha \mid v(\alpha_v) \le \exp(E_v) \text{ for all } v\}$ inside $\prod_v F$ by the submodule generated by $\{\alpha \in \mathbb{A} \mid v(\alpha_v) \le \exp(D_v)\}$ together with the image of the diagonal map $F \to \prod_v F$ is a finite $K$-module; and second, its $K$-dimension $i(D)$ satisfies $i(D) = \ell(D) - (\deg D + 1 - \gamma)$ in $\mathbb{Z}$. The integer $\gamma$ is produced existentially and is not asserted to equal $\gamma_0$.
--
--   This is the adelic form of the Riemann–Roch theorem, $\ell(D) - i(D) = \deg D + 1 - \gamma$, with $\gamma$ the Stichtenoth genus defined by the maximality property in the hypothesis; the index of specialty is computed as the $K$-dimension of the adele class group attached to $D$. It is used to obtain the same conclusion from the curve axioms alone and to extract the uniform bound $\deg D + 1 - \ell(D) \le \gamma$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicCurve_exists_genus_riemannIndex_of_stichtenothGenusExists.lean

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_AlgebraicCurve_DivisorClassGroup
import Definitions.Def_AlgebraicCurve_Repartitions
import Definitions.Def_AlgebraicCurve_IsCurveOver
import Definitions.Def_AlgebraicCurve_AdelicIndex

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

namespace AlgebraicCurve

theorem exists_genus_riemannIndex_of_stichtenothGenusExists {K F : Type*} [Field K] [Field F] [Algebra K F] [IsCurveOver K F]
    (h : StichtenothGenusExists K F) :
    ∃ γ : ℤ, ∀ D : Divisor K F,
      Module.Finite K (↥(adeleSpace K F) ⧸ adeleBddPrincipal K F D) ∧
        (indexOfSpecialty D : ℤ) = (ell D : ℤ) - (Divisor.degree D + 1 - γ) := by sorry
